{
  "_comment": [
    "Webhook request bodies byte for byte as the gateway builds them, one per",
    "payload shape. Each suite signs these and parses them, so the two clients",
    "are held to the same bytes rather than to each one's idea of the shape.",
    "",
    "The gateway marshals the envelope with encoding/json, not protojson, and so",
    "does each payload: field names are snake_case, a delivery event's type is",
    "the EmailEventType NUMBER, and an inbound message's timestamp is",
    "{\"seconds\", \"nanos\"} rather than a string. Those are the gateway's Go",
    "struct tags (internal/event/repositories/entities.EmailEvent,",
    "internal/emailfilter.HeldEvent and OutcomeEvent, panmailv1.InboundEmail), not",
    "the protos, so scripts/check-proto-drift.sh cannot see them change.",
    "",
    "Produced by marshalling those types at gateway commit 407f95d (main) with",
    "the envelope internal/webhook/worker.DurableWorker.Enqueue writes. There is no",
    "script for it: the types are internal to the gateway, so a generator has to",
    "run inside its module. Regenerate by hand when those types change."
  ],
